SUMMARY:SABEW Canada Best in Business Awards Celebration
DESCRIPTION:Come recognize excellence\, celebrate with your friends and colleagues\, and indulge in a little healthy competition at SABEW Canada’s annual Best in Business Awards. Food and two drink tickets are included with your registration. \nRegister by 11:59 p.m. ET\, May 21\, to take advantage of the early-bird price of $40 (USD). Once the early-bird deadline passes\, the registration fee will then be $45 (USD). \nWhen: Thursday\, May 28\, 2026\, 7 p.m.\nWhere: The Pilot\, 22 Cumberland St.\, Toronto\nHow: Complete the form below to purchase tickets
URL:https://sabew.org/event/sabew-canada-best-in-business-awards-celebration-2/
CATEGORIES:Best in Business,SABEW Canada
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260529T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260529T140000
DTSTAMP:20260524T230911
CREATED:20260521T174254Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260521T175100Z
UID:71293-1780059600-1780063200@sabew.org
SUMMARY:AI in medical devices: Hype or cost savings? webinar
DESCRIPTION:One of the fastest-growing businesses is integrating AI into all of our medical devices\, from those watch apps to ultrasound machines and medical charts.  How can we get beyond the hype to see what works and what’s bunk? And how can we see if our local hospitals are buying dreams or real patient care? \nThis webinar is in partnership with The National Institute for Health Care Management (NIHCM) Foundation. \nPanelists: \n\nFerdous Al-Faruque\, senior editor\, Regulatory Focus\nKatie Palmer\, health tech reporter\, STAT\n\nModerator: \n\nMarty Steffens\, University of Missouri and SABEW chair for business and financial Journalism\n\nRegistration: \nThis is a free webinar\, but you must register below to receive the Zoom link. The link will be sent to all registrants before the event.
URL:https://sabew.org/event/ai-in-medical-devices-hype-or-cost-savings-webinar/
CATEGORIES:Virtual Training
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://sabew.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/May-2026-NIHCM-Webinar-Graphic.jpg
END:VEVENT
